{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "def truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Return the fractional part of the strictly positive float 'number'.\n    The fractional part is in [0.0, 1.0).\n    Doctest:\n    >>> truncate_number(3.5)\n    0.5\n    \"\"\"\n    if type(number) is not float:\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'number' must be an exact Python float.\")\n    if number <= 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'number' must be strictly positive (> 0.0).\")\n    import math\n    fractional_part, _ = math.modf(number)\n    return fractional_part"}
